00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:55.700
Now for a quick grammar bite. In Russian nouns have gender. They can be masculine, feminine or neuter.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.080
This changes the endings of words that describe them.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:06.060
Take the word racketa, which is feminine. We say a big racketa for a big racket.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:15.900
The word cosmos is masculine, so we say a big cosmos. And the word sunset is neuter, so we say a big sunset.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:25.140
In English, the word big stays the same no matter what. But in Russian, the ending changes so the words fit together nicely.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:32.400
This helps you describe things in space. In our culture corner, Russia has a special place in space history.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:44.240
The Soviet Union launched the first satellites putnik in 1957. Then in 1961, Yuri Gagarin became the first human to orbit the Earth.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:52.900
Russians often call space travelers cosmonauts. Space exploration is taught in schools as something full of wonder.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:05:00.460
